  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>prctile</keyword>
  <short_description>Percentiles of a data set.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>P = prctile(A, pct)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>P = prctile(A, pct, dim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>P = prctile(A, pct, vecdim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>P = prctile(A, pct, 'all')</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>P = prctile(..., 'Method', method)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>prctile</b> returns percentiles for percentages in the interval [0,100].</p>
    <p><b>NaN</b> values are omitted. Supported methods are <b>midpoint</b>, <b>exact</b>, <b>inclusive</b>, <b>exclusive</b>, and <b>approximate</b>.</p>
    <p><b>A</b> can be a real numeric array, a <b>datetime</b> array or a <b>duration</b> array. For datetime or duration input data, <b>P</b> has the same class and Format as <b>A</b>, and <b>NaT</b> values are omitted like <b>NaN</b> values.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[A = (1:5)' * (2:6);
P = prctile(A, [25 50 75], 1)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>datetime and duration input data</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[t = datetime(2024, 1, [1 3 5 7 30]);
P = prctile(t, [25 50 75])]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
